{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require an evidence-based review of health programmes before public broadcast",
        "additional_details": "Ofcom doesn't approve shows before broadcast and the rules do not require independent review before release. We want prevention and post-release enforcement to improve public information. Misleading health claims can affect stigma, help-seeking and treatment decisions.",
        "background": "We want the Government to amend media law so that factual TV and on-demand programmes, that make significant health or medical claims, undergo documented review by suitably qualified, independent experts before they are released to the public.",
